---
import '../styles/space.css';
import ConclusionMark from '../components/ConclusionMark.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const url = (path: string) => base + '/' + path + '/';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head>
  <meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/>
  <meta name="description" content="The contingency argument for a necessary mental foundation."/>
  <title>X → G</title>
  <link rel="icon" href={base + '/favicon.svg'} />
  <script is:inline src={base + '/reading-transition.js'}></script>
</head><body class="argument-page">
<main>
  <h1>X → G</h1>
  <section id="preface"><h2 aria-label="Supplementary Argument — The Brute-Factuality Challenge"><span class="sideways-s" aria-hidden="true">S</span></h2>
    <p><span class="premise">S1.</span> A <a href={url('terms/brute-fact')}>brute fact</a> is a fact whose obtaining lacks a sufficient explanation.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">S2.</span> To assert that a fact is brute, you need independent grounds for claiming that it lacks a sufficient explanation.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">S3.</span> <a href={url('terms/presupposing-inexplicability')}>Presupposing inexplicability</a> assumes the claim that requires justification.</p>
    <p>The absence of a known explanation does not establish that no explanation exists.</p>
    <p><ConclusionMark n={1} supplementary /> A categorical appeal to <a href={url('terms/brute-existence')}>brute existence</a> or <a href={url('terms/brute-emergence')}>brute emergence</a> requires independent justification.</p>
    <p><ConclusionMark n={2} supplementary /> Merely proposing brute existence does not refute the argument for necessary grounding.</p>
    <p>You can suspend judgment about brute factuality without accepting the argument’s conclusion.</p>
    <p>That suspension, however, does not establish that your assertion is right and the assertion of explicability in any such case is wrong.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="dependence"><h2><a href={url('argument/contingency')}>I</a></h2>
    <p><span class="premise">P1.</span> Something <a href={url('terms/contingent-existence')}>exists contingently</a>.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P2.</span> If a thing’s <a href={url('terms/intrinsic-nature')}>intrinsic nature</a> fully grounds its existence, then it exists necessarily.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P3.</span> Whatever exists contingently could have failed to exist.</p>
    <p><ConclusionMark n={1} /> A contingent existent lacks a wholly intrinsic sufficient ground of existence.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P4.</span> A sufficient ground of existence is either wholly intrinsic or at least partly external.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P5.</span> The <a href={url('terms/restricted-principle-of-sufficient-reason')}>restricted Principle of Sufficient Reason</a> states that every contingent existent has a sufficient explanation of its existence.</p>
    <p><ConclusionMark n={2} /> Every contingent existent has an external <a href={url('terms/ground')}>ground</a> of existence.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="necessity"><h2><a href={url('argument/necessity')}>II</a></h2>
    <p><span class="premise">P6.</span> At least one existent depends on a ground beyond itself.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P7.</span> The <a href={url('terms/dependent-totality')}>dependent totality</a> has a complete ground.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P8.</span> Each explanation that appeals to another dependent existent presupposes that dependent reality exists.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P9.</span> A complete explanation of why dependent reality exists cannot presuppose that dependent reality exists.</p>
    <p><ConclusionMark n={3} /> The complete ground of dependent reality <a href={url('objections/the-dependent-totality')}>includes an independent existent</a>.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P10.</span> An independent existent has no external ground of existence.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P11.</span> Every actual existent is either contingent or necessary.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P12.</span> An independent existent <a href={url('objections/independent-but-contingent')}>cannot be contingent</a>, since C2 would give it an external ground.</p>
    <p><ConclusionMark n={4} /> At least one <a href={url('terms/independent-ground')}>independent ground</a> of dependent reality has <a href={url('terms/necessary-existence')}>necessary existence</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="mind"><h2><a href={url('argument/mind')}>III</a></h2>
    <p><span class="premise">P13.</span> The <a href={url('terms/actual-concrete-order')}>actual concrete order</a> is contingent.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P14.</span> If a necessary foundation <a href={url('terms/necessitation')}>necessitates the actual order</a>, then that order is necessary.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P15.</span> An exclusively <a href={url('terms/impersonal')}>impersonal</a> <a href={url('terms/ultimate-ground')}>ultimate ground</a> either <a href={url('terms/necessitation--p15')}>necessitates its outcome</a> or produces it through <a href={url('terms/impersonal-indeterminism')}>impersonal indeterminism</a>.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P16.</span> No necessary foundation <a href={url('terms/necessitation--p16')}>necessitates the actual order</a>, given P13 and P14.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P17.</span> A complete ground of the actual order supplies a <a href={url('terms/contrastive-explanation')}>contrastive explanation</a> of its actuality.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P18.</span> An <a href={url('terms/impersonal--p18')}>impersonal</a> distribution can assign positive chances to distinct outcomes.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P19.</span> An <a href={url('terms/impersonal--p19')}>impersonal</a> distribution of chances <a href={url('objections/impersonal-chance')}>does not explain why this outcome occurred rather than another</a>.</p>
    <p><ConclusionMark n={5} /> An exclusively <a href={url('terms/impersonal--c5')}>impersonal</a> ground cannot completely explain why the actual order obtains.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P20.</span> Only <a href={url('terms/intentional-selection')}>intentional selection</a> can settle which order obtains while <a href={url('objections/selection-and-reasons')}>preserving the possibility of a different order</a>.</p>
    <p><span class="premise">P21.</span> Intentional selection requires the <a href={url('terms/representing-alternatives')}>capacity to represent alternatives</a>.</p>
    <p><ConclusionMark n={6} /> The <a href={url('terms/ultimate-ground--c6')}>ultimate ground</a> that settles which order obtains has mental capacity.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="conclusion"><h2><a href={url('argument/conclusion')}>IV</a></h2>
    <p><span class="premise">P22.</span> At least one <a href={url('terms/independent-ground--p22')}>independent ground</a> of dependent reality is itself the <a href={url('terms/ultimate-ground--p22')}>ultimate ground</a> that settles which order obtains.</p>
    <p><ConclusionMark n={7} /> Contingent reality has a necessary mental foundation.</p>
    <a class="proof" href={url('examination/proof')}>Formal logical proof</a>
  </section>
</main></body></html>
<style>
  :global(*){box-sizing:border-box}
  body{margin:0;color:#e6e6e8;font:500 1.125rem/1.7 Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif}
  main{margin:auto;max-width:46rem;padding:clamp(3rem,8vw,7rem) 1.45rem 5rem}
  h1,h2,p{margin:0}h1{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,6.5vw,4.7rem);font-weight:400;line-height:1.03;letter-spacing:-.05em;text-wrap:balance;margin-bottom:2.4rem}
  h1,p{-webkit-text-stroke:.012em currentColor}
  section+section{margin-top:2.75rem}
  h2 a,h2 a:hover,h2 a:focus-visible{text-decoration:none}
  h2{font:600 .92rem/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;margin-bottom:1rem}
  p+p{margin-top:.8rem}a{color:inherit;text-decoration-color:#78787d;text-underline-offset:.19em;text-decoration-thickness:1px}
  a:hover,a:focus-visible{text-decoration-color:white;color:white}
  a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #fff;outline-offset:3px}
  .sideways-s{display:inline-block;transform:rotate(90deg);font:600 1.1rem/1 system-ui,sans-serif}
  .premise{font:600 .75em/1 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#bebec4;-webkit-text-stroke:0}
  .proof{font: .9rem system-ui,sans-serif;display:inline-block;margin-top:1rem}
</style>
